# Disabled is a local override: CMS Events never clear it, only an Admin does.
@run = 1
@id = disable-{{run}}

### Publish v1
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T10:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Controversial" } }
]

### A User can't disable: 403
PATCH {{host}}/entities/{{id}}/disable
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### Admin disables: 200, disabledBy admin
PATCH {{host}}/entities/{{id}}/disable
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### User: 404
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### CMS publishes v2: applies, but stays Disabled
POST {{host}}/cms/events
Authorization: Basic {{cmsUsername}} {{cmsPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "type": "publish", "id": "{{id}}", "version": 2, "timestamp": "2026-01-01T11:00:00Z", "payload": { "title": "Toned down" } }
]

### Admin: version 2, isDisabledByAdmin true
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### Admin enables: 200
PATCH {{host}}/entities/{{id}}/enable
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}

### User: version 2 visible again
GET {{host}}/entities/{{id}}
Authorization: Basic {{readerUsername}} {{readerPassword}}

### Disable an unknown id: 404
PATCH {{host}}/entities/unknown-{{run}}/disable
Authorization: Basic {{adminUsername}} {{adminPassword}}
